(MC3)

This version (which will not match the recording as it's in the easier to play key of (G) is for fingerstyle and is pretty easy to play.  The notations in brackets with small case letters, like <g> or <pull> are meant as a reminder to pluck a note or remove a finger.  These notes will the notes transpose correctly unless you remove the parenthesis.  

TIP:  The intro is repeated at the end of each verse. (A7G) is simply (A7) with pinky on the 1st string (<g> note).  The (A7sus4) is sandwiched between two (Am7)s and is struck just once so just keep the (Am7) position and put your pinky on the 2nd string/3rd fret. 

TIP:  To play the (CaddD) just keep the (C) formation and add pinky to 2nd string/3rd fret.  In the second line - only time it occurs - you start with (CaddD) then go to (C) by removing the pinky, then to (Cmaj7) by removing the index finger.  Easy.

TIP:  It's important to add the bass <g> (top string) when playing the (C/G) at the end of the verse after "love".

TIP:  In the third verse there is a (Em) (C/B) (E7full) (Em) progression.  When moving from (Em) to (C/B) you just add the index finger to 2nd string/1st fret.  Then to play the (E7) you can keep your index finger as is and put your pinky on 2nd string/3rd fret while removing your ring finger (but it also sounds just fine if you leave the ring finger where it is in the (Em) position as you're going right back to that chord anyway).  Suggest you rehearse this line a couple of times.      
   
          
